From c4b7ca468c0972d61342e7305b867715e7d8bba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:52:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Turn the address bar into a tab search as the tab sheet
 opens.

In Sheet mode the address bar crossfades into a Search tabs field as the
sheet is pulled open, in step with the sheet's progress, and back into the
address bar, URL intact, as it closes. The field is drawn over the toolbar
in the activity window; the omnibox is not touched.

Typing filters the sheet's list or grid live by every word of the title or
address; clearing lists every tab again. Focusing the field takes the sheet
full and keeps it open, and the sheet and field stay above the keyboard,
with or without glass. Back hides the keyboard, then clears the search,
then closes the sheet. Reordering is off while a filter is shown. Top
address bar mirrors this at the top. The side drawer is unchanged.

Tested on the Android emulator (Pixel 10 Pro profile).
